From 4d6696ff539c2cd05fe4ae4c6df7e037f952d4f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:33:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] steam-frame client: review hardening and the sRGB double
 encode (2026-10-21)

Adversarial review of the client, 2026-10-21. Fixes, in the order of the findings:

- H1: the video carries gamma-encoded values (the server re-encodes linear to sRGB before VideoToolbox) and the
  R8G8B8A8_SRGB swapchain encoded them again on store, so the compositor was handed sRGB(sRGB(x)). The shader now
  linearises when the attachment is an sRGB format (push constant srgbTarget). FRAME_CLIENT_SRGB_LINEARIZE=0 restores
  the old picture for an A/B.
- H2: the worn defaults live in the binary: PREDICT_MS 40, PREDICT_POS 0, PREDICT_POS_MS 40, STAMP_POS_LIVE 1,
  deadband off. The launcher no longer has to set them.
- H3/H4: video datagrams from any address other than the server are dropped (FRAME_CLIENT_ACCEPT_ANY_SOURCE=1 to
  allow); headers with totalPackets 0 or above 4096, payloadSize above the packet payload, or a data packetIndex
  past totalPackets are dropped before the assembler sizes anything; the access unit is capped at 2 MB (cleared and a
  keyframe requested on overflow).
- H5: render poses off the wire are checked finite, within 100 m and a unit quaternion within 10 percent, then
  normalised; xrEndFrame failures are logged (rate limited).
- H6: with FRAME_CLIENT_SERVER pinned, only that address's announce is accepted.
- H7: the discovery result is copied under a mutex and published after the copy; StopDiscovery wakes the recvfrom
  with shutdown and joins the thread, so nothing writes into the caller's frame after Connect returns.
- H8: Stop shuts the sockets down, joins, then closes (close alone does not wake a blocked recv on Linux).
- M1: Ctrl-C leaves the loop when the exit request fails or EXITING does not come within 3 s.

692 unit checks pass. Built on the headset; not yet worn.
